Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.44,0:00:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's look at how IncidentLens works under the\Nhood. It runs as a centralized LangGraph workflow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.57,0:00:09.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Starting from a public incident summary, the\NCoordinator inspects the current evidence gaps
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.52,0:00:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,and remaining budget, then dynamically\Ndispatches one or two specialists per round:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.21,0:00:17.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Logs for error chronology, Metrics\Nfor capacity and dependencies,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.16,0:00:21.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Database for locks, connections, and slow queries,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.41,0:00:26.22,Default,,0,0,0,,and Changes for recent deployments and config\Ndiffs. Two safeguards keep the workflow honest.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.44,0:00:30.12,Default,,0,0,0,,First, strict tool ACL isolation—for example,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.47,0:00:35.72,Default,,0,0,0,,the Logs agent can never query config diffs.\NSecond, a deterministic FinalizeGate:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.15,0:00:40.06,Default,,0,0,0,,final acceptance never relies on\Nan LLM's self-reported confidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.34,0:00:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Instead, deterministic code verifies\Nat least two independent sources,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.44,0:00:48.97,Default,,0,0,0,,a cause-specific discriminator,\Ntemporally compatible impact,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.25,0:00:52.37,Default,,0,0,0,,and zero unresolved contradictions\Nor rival mechanisms.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.71,0:00:56.40,Default,,0,0,0,,To evaluate whether dynamic multi-agent\Norchestration actually pays off,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.40,0:01:01.90,Default,,0,0,0,,we compare four architectures under\Nidentical budgets and equivalent tool access:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.35,0:01:07.44,Default,,0,0,0,,a Single-agent baseline, a one-shot Fixed-4\Nbatch, our primary Dynamic architecture,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.44,0:01:11.49,Default,,0,0,0,,and Full, which adds an\Nindependent LLM Verifier loop.
